d at assessing weather, excellent computer skills, weak memory for numbers, makes nasty remarks, grumpy, uncooperative.\n\nCandidate C: anticipates dangerous situations, sees complex connections, excellent spatial vision, very good leadership qualities, sometimes not good at taking criticism, can be unorganized, not open to new ideas, regarded as show-off.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, concentrates very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, arrogant, weak leadership, hot temper, know-it-all.\n\nWe need to consider criteria: reliability, technical competence, calmness under pressure, cooperation, responsibility, adaptability/feedback orientation.\n\nWe have concerns: A communication difficulty, egocentric, not willing to further education (adaptability). B nasty remarks, uncooperative, weak memory for numbers (attention). C not open to new ideas, show-off, unorganized, not good at criticism. D arrogant, hot temper, weak leadership.\n\nWe need to decide which candidate best overall. Let's weigh.\n\nReliability: A 100% reliable. B very conscientious (reliable). C? Not mentioned. D? Takes responsibility seriously (reliable). So A and B strong.\n\nTechnical competence: A quick correct decisions, technical understanding, excellent attention. B good at weather assessment, computer skills, but weak memory for numbers. C sees complex connections, spatial vision, leadership. D problem solving, concentration.\n\nCalmness under pressure: A calm in crisis. B handles stress well. C anticipates dangerous situations (maybe). D responds adequately.\n\nCooperation: A creates positive atmosphere with crew, puts concern for others above everything. B makes nasty remarks, uncooperative. C leadership but show-off, not open to new ideas. D arrogant, hot temper.\n\nResponsibility: A reliable, but not explicit. B conscientious. D takes responsibility seriously. C leadership.\n\nAdaptability/feedback: A not willing to further education (low). B unknown. C not open to new ideas, not good at criticism (low). D unknown but know-it-all, hot temper (maybe low). So all have limited evidence.\n\nGiven that cooperation is critical, A seems strongest: positive crew atmosphere, concern for others, despite communication difficulty and egocentric. Egocentric may affect crew, but positive atmosphere suggests cooperation. Communication difficulty could be mitigated with training.\n\nB's cooperation issues are more severe: nasty remarks, uncooperative, grumpy. That could harm safety.\n\nThus I think A is best overall.\n\nWe need to reference prior discussion: Agent 2 argued B, Agent 3 argued A. We can say we align with Agent 3, and explain why A's strengths outweigh concerns, and why B's cooperation issues are more problematic than A's communication gaps.\n\nWe also need to possibly ask for missing info? But we can make argument now.\n\nThus vote for Candidate A.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
